  "decision": "hold: on the native-order arithmetic the 2x4 split is 1.0-2.0% slower than main on the three Q4 legs (short 79.51 -> 77.89, long 65.49 -> 64.35, longctx 45.84 -> 45.36 tok/s, BF16 unchanged, all ids identical, exact-order checks 0 mismatches). The +7-13% measured pre-rebase came from sharing x loads across rows in the plain float kernel; main's precise per-block chains are already issue-bound per row and the extra row state costs registers. Keep main's kernel; do not integrate.",
  "next": "What survives is the measurement: streaming table, per-dispatch floor, issue-bound diagnostics (verdict.json). A future Q4 decode gain needs fewer dispatches per token (fusing q/k/v and gate/up GEMVs, 174 -> ~78 per token against a ~30 us floor) rather than a new lane split."
